 "notes": "Episodes: S1 80 + calibration 800 + gate 2,480 = 3,360 (plus 80 gate-0 replay, not evidence); 0 LLM generation calls; wall time about 35 minutes on the box. Deviation, made after the calibration and before any gate cell: the prefix-identity check originally compared every recorded step up to 150, including steps after a case had ended (the next episode's auto-reset), and reported differences of 11-24; restricted to in-play steps the prefixes are bit-identical between processes (0.0), and the gate used the in-play check. It did not enter the calibration's selection. No calibration setting met bound activity <= 0.20 and feasible/requested >= 0.70, so the declared fallback chose cal2 by sign agreement (0.783; cal2 and cal3 identical). Post hoc, not pre-declared, from the recorded gate traces: (1) the split is by finger. Forefinger and ring finger track (sign agreement 0.994 and 1.000, bound activity 0.05 and 0.14, gains 0.21-0.92); middle finger and thumb do not (0.411 and 0.315), little finger is mostly bounded (0.899, bound activity 0.71). (2) The incumbent's own action is saturated at +/-1 on MFJ2 on 79% and LFJ1 on 64% (LFJ3 32%) of pulse-window steps, so an additive increment there is clipped; thumb-chain bounds are active on 0.89-0.98 of steps. (3) For mf_circumferential the pen surface point moves with the request (+0.52 of the requested speed) more than the fingertip does (+0.20), so the relative motion is opposite: that finger carries the pen. (4) Pulses changed no episode length: every pulse cell has the incumbent's 8 early drops and timeout rate 0.90, sustained successes 25-30 against 28. Unmeasured: contact forces; which individual bound was active (the trace stores their union); any request other than 0.02 m/s for 0.5 s at steps 150-180."
